      "content": "that's what they all say though. \"it's treatable,\" \"it's reversible.\" it just feels like people are saying that because they can't handle the alternative. but if someone really is just beyond help... if there's actually nothing left to salvage... isn't it just exhausting to keep pretending there is? it feels like there's a certain dignity in just accepting that you're done.",
